  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal&nbsp;fails to demonstrate it would&nbsp;be located within an appropriate location and would be of an acceptable design that would provide adequate space for the operations of a commercial unit.&nbsp;On this basis the application is&nbsp;contrary to:&nbsp;&nbsp;- The National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)-&nbsp;Policies&nbsp;D1, D4,&nbsp; and D5 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies DMD1, DMD6, DME3, SP5, and DME3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September, 2024)",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;By reasons of the site design and layout the proposal fails to&amp;nbsp;demonstrate it is of a suitable design for the commercial use. It has not been adequately demonstrated the the proposed unit would be suitably located within an existing residential site, with no clear separation identified. The application is therefore contrary to the outlined planning framework:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;- The National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies D4 London Plan (March 2021)&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies S1, SP2, SP5, DME3, DMD1,and&amp;nbsp; DMD4,&amp;nbsp;of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037&amp;nbsp;(September, 2024)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:</p><p>- DRAWING XXX REV XX DATED XX<br>- USE [SHIFT]+[ENTER] FOR REGULAR LINE SPACING<br>- USE [ENTER] FOR LARGER LINE SPACING</p><p>No other drawings or documents apply.</p>",
    "The application has failed to provide sufficient information to demonstrate&nbsp;that the proposal would not have a negative impact on the amenity of neighbouring residential properties. Specifically, the application has failed to provide sufficient information regarding the potential noise impacts due to increased coming and goings to the site or operations which may be harmful to the standard of living of neighbouring residents. The proposal is contrary to- The National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)-&nbsp;Policies GG3, D6 and D13, D14&nbsp;London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies DMD1 and DMSI3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037&nbsp;(September, 2024)"
  ],
